\[
\begin{pmatrix}
\cos\theta & -\sin\theta \\
\sin\theta & \cos\theta
\end{pmatrix}
\]
For a rotation clockwise by an angle of $45^\circ$, $\theta = -45^\circ$. Substituting $\theta = -45^\circ$ into the rotation matrix formula, we get:
\[
\begin{pmatrix}
\cos(-45^\circ) & -\sin(-45^\circ) \\
\sin(-45^\circ) & \cos(-45^\circ)
\end{pmatrix}
\]
